            <ArticleTitle>The role of the family physician in the care of the child with cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>258-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cancer in the child is no longer a death sentence. Although the treatment has become complex, the survival rate has increased impressively. Modern treatment involves a multidisciplinary approach, which should include the primary physician as a key member of the highly skilled treatment team.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
